---
import StudyLayout from "../../../layouts/StudyLayout.astro";
---

<StudyLayout>
  <section>
    <h1>Venus-like planets — question test</h1>
    <p>
      13 November 2026. Independent, clean-context, read-only review of the
      <a href="/lab/studies/venus-2026-11-13">study opening</a>, registry, study
      contract and relevant implementation.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>One subject — Pass.</strong>
      Cloud, light and motion are facets of one Venus-like body, inspectable
      together. The open Mercury study concerns airless rock; this cycle uses
      implemented Mercury as a comparison and does not reopen its design. No
      other registry question owns this visual decision.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Grounded — Pass.</strong>
      Fixed art direction and Practice references have specification and code
      support. Open properties can be exposed in a built visual example;
      blank-disc and luminous-energy readings are explicitly hypotheses.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Consequence — Pass.</strong>
      The result is one reusable Venus-like planet drawing demonstrated in the
      Lab. Placement of a named Venus in Practice remains a later decision.
    </p>
    <h2>Evidence and findings</h2>
    <p>
      No substantive findings required correction. The opening was retained.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>docs/design.md</code>, art direction: economical forms, convincing
        material and composed light for natural bodies.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>docs/specs/game/world/planets/spec.md</code>, Mercury contract;
        <code>packages/mode-a/src/lib/flight-frame.ts</code>, simulation-timed
        spin and Sun-facing light;
        <code>apps/web/src/components/FlightDeck.svelte</code>, Practice asset
        loading and rendering.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>docs/specs/game/test-flight/spec.md</code>
        and
        <code>docs/specs/game/world/star/spec.md</code>, G7 reference;
        <code>packages/mode-a/src/lib/simulation.ts</code>, Practice Sun and
        Mercury setup.
      </li>
      <li>
        Planet and gravity-field specifications plus
        <code>packages/core/src/lib/physics/Physics.ts</code>: orbital motion,
        planetary gravity and surface response.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>apps/web/src/data/studies.ts</code>: complete registry checked for
        ownership.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
      The reviewer did not check browser rendering, runtime asset loading,
      keyboard operation, viewport behaviour, visual success, gameplay feel,
      physical accuracy, implementation feasibility or performance. This is a
      question test, not a whole-study evaluation or design acceptance.
    </p>
  </section>
</StudyLayout>
